            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I have not certainly tested this, but instead of patching `${CARGO_HOME}/config.toml`, perhaps you could create an extra `my-config.toml` and pass `--config ${UNPACKDIR}/my-config.toml` to `cargo` [1] to override all the wrong key value and missing entries for workspace, etc?\n\nIf that works, that would remove the need for overriding those functions in `-git-crates.inc`. Sorta in a sense that we are providing our own `config.toml`, but just reusing some default toolchain values inherited from the `${CARGO_HOME}/config.toml`.\n\n[1] https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't find any existing recipe using `cargo --config extra.toml`.\n\nIn V3, I changed the generated config location from ${CARGO_HOME}/config.toml to ${S}/.cargo/config.toml instead of modifying the shared ${CARGO_HOME} configuration."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "@vince_chang@aspeedtech.com do you know when the V3 with the solution for all recipes will be available? I am keen on testing it out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vince Chang",
                        "email": "vince_chang@aspeedtech.com",
                        "username": "VinceChang6637"
                    },
                    "message": "Probably in July, after the next ASPEED SDK release.\nAlso, please note that caliptra-mcu-sw_git.bb may be renamed. The plan is for AST27x0 to use caliptra-mcu-sw_1x.bb, and AST27x5 to use a new recipe, caliptra-mcu-sw_2x.bb."
                }
            ],
